# Force LF line endings for every text file this repository tracks,
# regardless of a contributor's local core.autocrlf setting. Without this,
# a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true silently rewrites every
# checked-out file to CRLF while the repository itself still stores LF,
# which makes gofmt, golangci-lint, and "git diff" all report spurious
# differences that do not exist in what is actually committed or what CI
# (which runs on Linux) actually sees.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Keep Windows-only script files consuming their own working-directory
# checkout in the native line ending Windows expects, since existing
# tooling on Windows generally requires it.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary/opaque fixture and archive content must never be line-ending
# normalized.
*.esa binary
*.zip binary
*.jar binary
*.png binary
*.gif binary
